  "adaptations": [
    "The Go host binds ordinary Web, API, private once and public service scopes to the current instance. It pins official asset metadata, digest and executable build info. It invokes direct argv in the owned instance path, uses fresh result bytes and refuses unverified legacy binaries and invalid extraction. The v2.2.2 official assets retain the old name already mismatched by the installed source.",
    "The host updates only the source-allowed CustomHosts fields after checking the running registered peer, saved config stamp and exact selected-IP replacement. An unloaded peer follows the missing-hosts path. A queued reload is asynchronous, and a disabled CustomHosts follows the ordinary event eligibility rules.",
    "There is no recovered replay of a same-process interruption between saving both configs and admitting reload. The next unchanged-IP run follows source behavior and skips another reload. Private cache restart and complete commands were observed.",
    "The test-only peer proves separate worker dispatch and owned-file effects. Actual production-grade CustomHosts 1.2.2 is the next independent slice. Linux ARM64 packaging is supported by the engine host code but native runtime evidence is x86_64 only. Unreferenced direct Python Hosts methods were not imported."
  ],
